In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  Painters paint, varnish, wallpaper and other protective and decorative materials to interior and exterior walls and surfaces, painters also paint the interior and exterior of buildings and other structures. They may use standard latex based paints or specialised paints for decorative effect or protective properties. Painters are skilled in using brushes, paint rollers and paint sprayers for different applications. 


Tasks required by this job include:

- erects working platform or scaffolding up to five metres in height;
- prepares surfaces by cleaning, sanding and filling cracks and holes with appropriate filler;
- applies primer, undercoat and finishing coat(s) using brush, roller, or spray equipment;
- mixes adhesive or removes self-adhesive backing and positions covering material on wall, matching up patterns where appropriate and removing wrinkles and air bubbles by hand or brush;
- stains, waxes and french polishes wood surfaces by hand.

In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  Due to continued expansion, Flynn Transport Ltd is looking for 3 fully Qualified and experienced HGV Drivers to join the team in Ireland. This is a full time, permanent position based out of the Dublin yard, D18 C5C8.
Salary: €47000 - €54000 per annum, dependent on experience.
45 hrs/wk
Duties include, but are not limited to:
Checks tyres, brakes, lights, oil, water and fuel levels and general condition of the vehicle;
Drives vehicle from depot to loading/unloading point;
Agrees delivery schedule and route with transport management;
Drives vehicle to destination in accordance with schedule;
Maintains records of journey times, mileage and hours worked;
Ensures that load is evenly distributed and safely secured;
Undertakes minor repairs and notifies supervisor of any mechanical faults.
Requirements:
Fluent in English
Minimum 5+ years HGV driving experience

